## Root `.gitignore` — `automation/` (MANDATORY)

Applies to **every** task (scaffold, feature work, test-case generation, Playwright setup). Do this at the **repository / monorepo root** before or when `automation/` exists.

| Rule | Requirement |
|------|-------------|
| File exists | **MUST** have a root `.gitignore`. **Create** `.gitignore` at repo root if it is missing. |
| `automation/` | **MUST** include `automation/` so the Playwright/QA automation tree is never committed. |
| Must not | **MUST NOT** commit `automation/` or remove the `automation/` ignore entry to force-commit specs/logs. |

**Required entry** (add if absent; do not duplicate):

```gitignore
# Playwright automation (generated locally for QA; do not commit)
automation/
```

**Agent checklist**

- [ ] Root `.gitignore` exists (created if missing)
- [ ] Contains `automation/` (with trailing slash)
- [ ] `automation/` is not tracked in git
