## 🔷 TypeScript Standards

### Key Rules (from typescript-stack.mdc)
- ✅ `"strict": true` in tsconfig; `tsc --noEmit` in CI
- ✅ No `any`—use `unknown` at boundaries, then narrow
- ✅ Explicit return types on public APIs
- ✅ Validate external input with Zod/schema (no blind `as` casts)
- ✅ `import type` for type-only imports
- ✅ `catch (err: unknown)` and narrow before use
- ✅ `noFloatingPromises` / async lint enabled
- ✅ Props typed explicitly in `.tsx` components

### Pattern
```typescript
// ✅ CORRECT
const body: unknown = await res.json()
const user = userSchema.parse(body)

export async function fetchUser(id: string): Promise<User> {
  const res = await fetch(`/api/users/${id}`)
  if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`HTTP ${res.status}`)
  return userSchema.parse(await res.json())
}

function getMessage(err: unknown): string {
  if (err instanceof Error) return err.message
  return 'Unknown error'
}

// ✗ NEVER DO THIS
const user = (await res.json()) as User
catch (e: any) { /* ... */ }
// @ts-ignore
const x = process.env.API_KEY!
```

