## 🍃 MongoDB Standards

### Key Rules (from mongodb-stack.mdc)
- ✅ Embed vs reference decided per collection (bounded vs shared/unbounded)
- ✅ `createdAt` / `updatedAt` on mutable docs; consistent soft delete
- ✅ `Decimal128` or integer cents for money (not float)
- ✅ Compound indexes: equality → sort → range; `explain` on hot paths
- ✅ Projections on reads; keyset pagination (no deep `skip`)
- ✅ One `MongoClient` per process; repositories only (not routes)
- ✅ Least-privilege user + TLS in production
- ✅ Parameterized filters—never user-controlled query keys
- ✅ Versioned migrations in `db/migrations/mongodb/`

### Pattern
```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT — index, projection, repository access
db.orders.createIndex({ userId: 1, createdAt: -1 })

export async function listOrders(userId, cursor, limit = 20) {
  const filter = { userId: new ObjectId(userId), deletedAt: null }
  if (cursor) filter.createdAt = { $lt: cursor }
  return orders.find(filter, {
    projection: { status: 1, totalCents: 1, createdAt: 1 },
  }).sort({ createdAt: -1 }).limit(limit).toArray()
}

// ✗ NEVER DO THIS
orders.find({ userId }).skip(page * 500).limit(20)  // deep skip
orders.find({ [field]: value })                       // injection-style keys
new MongoClient(uri) per request                      // pool exhaustion
{ price: 19.99 }                                      // float money
```

