## 🐘 PHP Standards

### Key Rules (from php-stack.mdc)
- ✅ PHP 8.2+ with `declare(strict_types=1)` on new files
- ✅ PSR-4 + Composer; `composer.lock` committed
- ✅ Only `public/` web-accessible; `.env` never in repo
- ✅ Controller → service → repository layering
- ✅ Typed parameters, returns, and properties; enums for fixed sets
- ✅ PDO/ORM prepared statements only (no SQL concat)
- ✅ Never `SELECT *`—list only needed columns (`SELECT id, email, ...`)
- ✅ `password_hash` / `password_verify` for passwords
- ✅ Form Request / Validator at boundary; central exception mapping
- ✅ `composer audit` in CI; `APP_DEBUG=false` in production

### Pattern
```php
<?php

declare(strict_types=1);

// ✅ CORRECT — strict types, bound query, typed service
$stmt = $pdo->prepare('SELECT id, email FROM users WHERE email = :email');
$stmt->execute(['email' => $email]);
$user = $stmt->fetch(PDO::FETCH_ASSOC);

// ✗ NEVER DO THIS
$pdo->query("SELECT * FROM users WHERE email = '$email'");
User::create(request()->all());           // mass assignment risk
echo $_GET['name'];                        // XSS
@file_get_contents($userPath);             // suppressed errors
eval($userCode);                           // code injection
```

