## 📱 Flutter Standards

### Key Rules (from flutter-stack.mdc)
- ✅ Sound null safety; avoid unnecessary `!`
- ✅ Feature-first `lib/` layout; thin `main.dart`
- ✅ `const` widgets where values are stable
- ✅ `ListView.builder` / slivers for long lists
- ✅ One state-management pattern per app (Riverpod, Bloc, or team standard)
- ✅ Loading, empty, and error UI for async screens
- ✅ Tokens in secure storage; HTTPS; no client secrets
- ✅ Widget + unit tests; integration tests for critical flows
- ✅ Honor `analysis_options.yaml` / `flutter_lints`

### Pattern
```dart
// ✅ CORRECT — const widget, typed model, bounded list
class UserList extends StatelessWidget {
  const UserList({super.key, required this.users});
  final List<User> users;

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return ListView.builder(
      itemCount: users.length,
      itemBuilder: (context, index) => UserTile(user: users[index]),
    );
  }
}

// ✗ NEVER DO THIS
Column(children: users.map((u) => UserTile(user: u)).toList()); // unbounded
final token = prefs.getString('token'); // insecure storage
```

